1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:02,100
<i> You caught the wrong person.</i>

2
00:00:02,233 --> 00:00:03,300
<i> This isn't right!</i>

3
00:00:03,433 --> 00:00:04,433
<i> What isn't right, Mom?</i>

4
00:00:04,567 --> 00:00:06,033
<i> Evil is just lurking around,</i>

5
00:00:06,167 --> 00:00:07,667
<i> isn't it?</i>

6
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:09,067
<i> Wait, I know this guy,</i>

7
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:11,133
<i>and Brother Tomas knows him too.</i>

8
00:00:11,267 --> 00:00:13,000
<i>Good thing that crook
didn't finish you off.</i>

9
00:00:13,133 --> 00:00:14,367
<i> He's ruthless, right?</i>

10
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:15,267
<i> We have no choice.</i>

11
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:16,333
<i> You'll be the one caught.</i>

12
00:00:16,467 --> 00:00:18,000
<i>- You'll be Berdugo.
- What?</i>

13
00:00:18,133 --> 00:00:19,267
<i> Surrender now, Berdugo!</i>

14
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:20,400
<i> You have nowhere to go!</i>

15
00:00:20,533 --> 00:00:21,667
<i> That's what you think.</i>

16
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:23,033
<i>Even when I was right
in front of you,</i>

17
00:00:23,167 --> 00:00:25,033
<i>you still couldn't do anything.</i>

18
00:00:25,167 --> 00:00:26,400
<i> I'm sorry, Liza.</i>

19
00:00:26,533 --> 00:00:28,167
<i> I will miss you.</i>

20
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:30,700
<i>Nice to meet the daughter
of the bravest man I know.</i>

21
00:00:30,833 --> 00:00:32,800
<i>I think I've heard
that voice before.</i>

22
00:00:32,933 --> 00:00:34,333
<i> I just can't remember where.</i>

23
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:37,033
<i>Everything is not what it seems.</i>

24
00:00:37,167 --> 00:00:40,433
<i>Don't stop until
you get to the truth.</i>

25
00:00:40,567 --> 00:00:43,367
<i> No, this is not Berdugo.</i>

26
00:00:46,733 --> 00:00:49,000
<i> [OBB]</i>

27
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:08,233
Oppa, what now?
I missed you!

28
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:09,733
This?

29
00:01:09,867 --> 00:01:11,367
Chips.

30
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:12,867
Are you okay?

31
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,067
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

32
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:17,367
Why? Aren't you happy to see us?

33
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:19,767
No, it's not that.

34
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:21,600
We have a problem.

35
00:01:21,733 --> 00:01:23,100
What is it?

36
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:26,000
This...

37
00:01:26,133 --> 00:01:27,800
That's Berdugo.

38
00:01:27,933 --> 00:01:29,233
He, has a problem, not us.

39
00:01:29,367 --> 00:01:30,600
He'll be jailed.

40
00:01:30,733 --> 00:01:32,033
The problem is...

41
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:34,500
this is not Berdugo.

42
00:01:34,633 --> 00:01:36,633
They got the wrong guy.

43
00:01:36,767 --> 00:01:38,233
Are you sure?
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

44
00:01:38,367 --> 00:01:40,167
Yes, one hundred percent,

45
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:41,733
because I have seen him before.

46
00:01:42,767 --> 00:01:44,533
<i> Stop this nonsense!</i>

47
00:01:44,667 --> 00:01:46,567
<i>Is this how you are
when I'm not here?</i>

48
00:01:46,700 --> 00:01:48,367
<i> Their tempers just flared up.</i>

49
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:50,467
<i>I promise this is the first
and last time</i>

50
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:51,533
<i> that this will happen.</i>

51
00:01:51,667 --> 00:01:52,667
<i> I hope so.</i>

52
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:55,867
<i> Because if not, I'll fix it,</i>

53
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,533
<i> and I promise you...</i>

54
00:01:57,667 --> 00:01:59,467
<i> you won't like it.</i>

55
00:02:00,367 --> 00:02:01,900
I don't know his real name.

56
00:02:02,033 --> 00:02:04,033
But I got a good look
at his face.

57
00:02:04,167 --> 00:02:05,533
I can identify him.

58
00:02:06,667 --> 00:02:08,467
If only I can see him again.

59
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:11,767
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

60
00:02:16,067 --> 00:02:19,067
And of course,
we would like to recognize

61
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:23,700
the person responsible
for the rescue of my husband

62
00:02:23,833 --> 00:02:27,067
and the capture
of the notorious Berdugo,

63
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:30,033
Major Miguel Delgado.

64
00:02:30,167 --> 00:02:34,200
- [APPLAUDING]
- [CAMERA SHUTTER SNAPPING]

65
00:02:35,267 --> 00:02:39,233
On behalf of our Hope Circle
Foundation,

66
00:02:39,367 --> 00:02:43,033
please accept
this People's Medal of Honor.

67
00:02:44,167 --> 00:02:48,200
[CROWD APPLAUDING]

68
00:02:49,067 --> 00:02:53,667
You have no idea the impact this
has on me, Major Delgado.

69
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:57,400
Because of you,
we no longer fear Berdugo.

70
00:02:57,533 --> 00:03:01,467
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

71
00:03:02,633 --> 00:03:04,500
Why, Major? Is there...

72
00:03:04,633 --> 00:03:06,067
a problem?

73
00:03:06,667 --> 00:03:08,733
You know, Sir, I feel...

74
00:03:09,467 --> 00:03:11,633
Even if we caught Berdugo,

75
00:03:12,233 --> 00:03:14,400
his viciousness is still around.

76
00:03:14,533 --> 00:03:18,600
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

77
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:21,967
Look at this report.

78
00:03:22,133 --> 00:03:23,900
It looks like the other news
outlet has the same context...

79
00:03:24,033 --> 00:03:26,300
about Berdugo.

80
00:03:26,433 --> 00:03:28,733
Then let's change our approach!

81
00:03:28,867 --> 00:03:30,633
That's why people watch us,

82
00:03:30,767 --> 00:03:32,867
because we have our own take
on things.

83
00:03:33,700 --> 00:03:34,567
Yes, that's right.

84
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:36,033
Oh, I know.

85
00:03:36,533 --> 00:03:38,067
No one's interviewed...

86
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:39,133
Berdugo yet.

87
00:03:39,267 --> 00:03:41,700
What if we get
an exclusive interview?

88
00:03:41,833 --> 00:03:42,967
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

89
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:45,467
No, no, no, we can't do that.

90
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:48,167
We'd just glorify the criminal.

91
00:03:48,667 --> 00:03:50,833
What if we interview
the victim instead?

92
00:03:50,967 --> 00:03:52,000
Mr. Tomas?

93
00:03:52,133 --> 00:03:52,933
Oh...

94
00:03:53,067 --> 00:03:54,367
didn't your brotherinlaw

95
00:03:54,533 --> 00:03:56,500
work with Berdugo?

96
00:03:56,633 --> 00:03:58,967
That's why he was chosen
as the victim.

97
00:03:59,100 --> 00:04:00,100
Dude, that's great!

98
00:04:00,233 --> 00:04:01,933
- Right? Right?
- Yes, I like that.

99
00:04:02,067 --> 00:04:03,933
And the title's going
to be good, it could be...

100
00:04:04,067 --> 00:04:07,133
"From Friend to Foe: Berdugo
in the Eyes of the Victim."

101
00:04:07,267 --> 00:04:08,800
- Right? Old-school!
- Nice, nice.

102
00:04:08,933 --> 00:04:10,333
So old-school! Right, Boss Idol?

103
00:04:10,467 --> 00:04:11,900
That's right, Boss.

104
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:16,167
[PHONE RINGING]

105
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:17,700
Someone's calling me.

106
00:04:19,867 --> 00:04:20,667
<i> Hello?</i>

107
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:22,267
Hello, Andrew?

108
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:24,733
You need to come
to the hospital now!

109
00:04:25,933 --> 00:04:27,000
Why? Is there a problem?

110
00:04:27,133 --> 00:04:30,033
Oppa said something.

111
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:33,733
Jin Ho said the real Berdugo
hasn't been caught yet.

112
00:04:33,867 --> 00:04:36,033
What? Is this a joke?

113
00:04:36,167 --> 00:04:38,900
No, the police got the wrong
Bersugo.

114
00:04:40,067 --> 00:04:41,800
Okay, fine, I'll go there.

115
00:04:41,933 --> 00:04:43,233
Take care.

116
00:04:43,367 --> 00:04:47,533
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

117
00:04:57,167 --> 00:04:58,433
- Joey.
- Andrew.

118
00:04:58,567 --> 00:05:01,733
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

119
00:05:01,900 --> 00:05:04,333
Is it true, what you said?

120
00:05:04,467 --> 00:05:06,833
The police caught
a fake Berdugo?

121
00:05:08,267 --> 00:05:09,967
Yes.

122
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:12,367
I know the real Berdugo.

123
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:16,000
He is probably planning
his escape now.

124
00:05:16,133 --> 00:05:18,367
We need to stop him.

125
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:20,567
Berdugo is very sly.

126
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:22,800
And manipulative.

127
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:25,633
Matias just claimed
he was Berdugo

128
00:05:25,767 --> 00:05:27,500
because he was ordered
to say so.

129
00:05:28,067 --> 00:05:30,167
We were fooled
by the real Berdugo.

130
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:33,367
What are we going to do now?

131
00:05:34,567 --> 00:05:37,167
Joey, did you tell your dad?

132
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:38,433
We're just waiting
for the cartographer

133
00:05:38,567 --> 00:05:40,300
from the precinct.

134
00:05:40,433 --> 00:05:42,500
If only I can get out of here.

135
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:45,867
I will look for Berdugo myself.

136
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,767
He still needs to pay
for Liza's death.

137
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:54,000
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

138
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:11,833
Thank you again.

139
00:06:11,967 --> 00:06:13,267
Because of what you did...

140
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:16,467
my men had a morale booster.

141
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:17,900
It is our pleasure.

142
00:06:18,733 --> 00:06:19,767
So, Chief?

143
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:21,433
We'll go ahead.

144
00:06:21,567 --> 00:06:23,233
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

145
00:06:27,367 --> 00:06:30,367
Ah, Major Delgado,
you have a new case already?

146
00:06:30,967 --> 00:06:32,200
No, Sir.

147
00:06:32,333 --> 00:06:34,400
It's still the old case.

148
00:06:34,967 --> 00:06:37,300
Sorry, I just have something to
attend to.

149
00:06:38,267 --> 00:06:40,533
Thank you, Mr. Limjoco.

150
00:06:42,533 --> 00:06:44,333
Is the cartographer on the way?

151
00:06:44,467 --> 00:06:48,633
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

152
00:06:53,133 --> 00:06:54,967
Drink some water first.

153
00:06:55,100 --> 00:06:56,367
Oppa, calm down.

154
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:57,467
Thank you.

155
00:06:58,467 --> 00:07:00,400
The police are already on alert.

156
00:07:00,533 --> 00:07:03,200
I'm sure Berdugo will be found.

157
00:07:03,333 --> 00:07:04,233
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

158
00:07:04,367 --> 00:07:05,700
He won't get away.

159
00:07:08,933 --> 00:07:11,167
We also bought
your snacks for later.

160
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:14,700
We'll surely take time
searching for Berdugo.

161
00:07:14,867 --> 00:07:16,533
For now, think of details

162
00:07:16,667 --> 00:07:17,633
you can share

163
00:07:17,767 --> 00:07:20,167
to help us find him faster.

164
00:07:20,567 --> 00:07:21,933
You're right, Joey.

165
00:07:22,633 --> 00:07:24,633
I'll call my brother, Tomas.

166
00:07:24,767 --> 00:07:28,533
I'm sure he knows
if Matias has associates.

167
00:07:28,667 --> 00:07:30,500
Maybe one of those is Berdugo.

168
00:07:31,100 --> 00:07:32,533
I'll just call him.

169
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,200
<i> Mr. Limjoco also gave</i>

170
00:07:35,333 --> 00:07:37,500
<i> a message to the police.</i>

171
00:07:37,633 --> 00:07:38,667
That's him!

172
00:07:39,467 --> 00:07:43,533
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

173
00:07:45,333 --> 00:07:48,367
<i>Our policemen are our real
heroes.</i>

174
00:07:48,533 --> 00:07:49,700
<i> They give us.</i>

175
00:07:49,833 --> 00:07:51,200
That's him.

176
00:07:51,333 --> 00:07:53,233
That is the real Berdugo!

177
00:07:56,833 --> 00:07:58,667
Wait, are you sure, Oppa?

178
00:07:59,267 --> 00:08:02,033
That's Andrew's family.

179
00:08:02,167 --> 00:08:04,000
That's his brother-in-law.

180
00:08:05,700 --> 00:08:07,033
Brother-in-law?

181
00:08:08,700 --> 00:08:10,433
Your family...

182
00:08:10,567 --> 00:08:11,933
he's a criminal?

183
00:08:12,067 --> 00:08:16,033
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

184
00:08:17,933 --> 00:08:20,200
<i>Sorry, did you say food
business, Tomas?</i>

185
00:08:20,333 --> 00:08:21,800
<i>- Yes.
- But you told me before,</i>

186
00:08:21,967 --> 00:08:23,967
<i> your business was textiles.</i>

187
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:25,400
<i> Oh, right, textiles.</i>

188
00:08:25,533 --> 00:08:26,800
<i>That was another client
with a food business.</i>

189
00:08:26,933 --> 00:08:27,833
<i> My bad.</i>

190
00:08:27,967 --> 00:08:30,867
<i>Everything is not what it seems
to be.</i>

191
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:34,933
<i>Don't stop until
you get to the truth.</i>

192
00:08:35,067 --> 00:08:36,633
<i> Keep it to yourself.</i>

193
00:08:36,767 --> 00:08:39,533
<i> Don't even tell your sister.</i>

194
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:41,233
<i> Next to them,</i>

195
00:08:41,367 --> 00:08:44,000
<i>these criminal syndicates
are just small-fry.</i>

196
00:08:44,233 --> 00:08:46,367
That's why his voice
sounded familiar.

197
00:08:46,767 --> 00:08:47,833
Whose?

198
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:51,333
<i> You're in such a rush.</i>

199
00:08:51,467 --> 00:08:52,433
<i> Why?</i>

200
00:08:52,567 --> 00:08:55,933
<i> Are those people chasing you?</i>

201
00:08:56,100 --> 00:08:57,733
<i>They're just small-fry
competition.</i>

202
00:08:57,867 --> 00:09:00,267
I've heard Sir Tomas's
voice before!

203
00:09:00,867 --> 00:09:02,767
And what he said in his speech,

204
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:05,033
it's the same thing I heard him
say to Valmora

205
00:09:05,167 --> 00:09:07,567
when Delilah and Berdugo
faced off.

206
00:09:10,233 --> 00:09:13,133
I'm sure he's Berdugo.

207
00:09:13,567 --> 00:09:15,233
Okay, we don't have time.

208
00:09:15,367 --> 00:09:16,300
Let's tell the guards.

209
00:09:16,433 --> 00:09:17,667
No.

210
00:09:19,233 --> 00:09:21,667
Let me check on this first.
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

211
00:09:21,900 --> 00:09:22,900
Check what?

212
00:09:23,833 --> 00:09:25,200
I saw him.

213
00:09:25,333 --> 00:09:26,967
And Joey heard him.

214
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:28,167
For what?

215
00:09:28,333 --> 00:09:30,333
Are you going to warn
your family?

216
00:09:33,867 --> 00:09:36,500
My family has nothing
to do with this.

217
00:09:38,267 --> 00:09:38,900
And what you're saying,

218
00:09:39,033 --> 00:09:40,733
those are just rumors.

219
00:09:41,167 --> 00:09:42,867
We need solid evidence

220
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,100
if we don't want Berdugo
to escape.

221
00:09:47,367 --> 00:09:49,267
<i> The teddy bear...</i>

222
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:50,267
<i> In Ma'am Rebecca's room,</i>

223
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:51,700
<i> there's a teddy bear.</i>

224
00:09:51,833 --> 00:09:53,467
<i> And it has a spy camera.</i>

225
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:56,400
<i>I'm sure it recorded
what really happened.</i>

226
00:09:56,533 --> 00:09:58,633
<i>Did Ma'am Rebecca tell you that?</i>

227
00:09:58,867 --> 00:10:00,933
<i>That you shouldn't
trust Sir Tomas?</i>

228
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:04,500
<i>I don't know,
she kept warning me.</i>

229
00:10:04,733 --> 00:10:06,267
The spy cam.

230
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:07,800
What spy cam?

231
00:10:07,933 --> 00:10:10,333
When Ma'am Rebecca had a
heart attack,

232
00:10:10,467 --> 00:10:12,833
she warned Mom about Sir Tomas.

233
00:10:13,633 --> 00:10:14,667
Mom thinks it was

234
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:18,033
captured by the camera inside
the teddy bear.

235
00:10:19,167 --> 00:10:21,200
<i>Uncle Andrew, we need your help.</i>

236
00:10:21,333 --> 00:10:22,867
<i> Okay, what is this?</i>

237
00:10:23,367 --> 00:10:25,233
<i>You got this from
the teddy bear?</i>

238
00:10:25,367 --> 00:10:27,267
<i> Yes, Kisses found it.</i>

239
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:29,567
<i>Let's see if it works.
Hopefully, it works.</i>

240
00:10:30,967 --> 00:10:32,533
I know where that is.

241
00:10:33,833 --> 00:10:34,900
I'll go there.

242
00:10:35,067 --> 00:10:36,567
- I'll find it.
- All right.

243
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:37,433
Wait.

244
00:10:37,567 --> 00:10:39,667
Are we letting him go?

245
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:41,567
Yes, for evidence.

246
00:10:43,567 --> 00:10:45,667
But he's right, Andrew,
you can't stay long.

247
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:48,900
If you're not back in 3 hours,

248
00:10:49,033 --> 00:10:51,000
I'll tell Dad.

249
00:10:51,133 --> 00:10:52,667
Thank you.

250
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:59,200
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

251
00:11:04,367 --> 00:11:07,900
[ENGINE WHIRRING]

252
00:11:11,167 --> 00:11:14,933
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

253
00:11:34,067 --> 00:11:38,267
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

254
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,600
- [GUN FIRING]
- [TOMAS GROANS]

255
00:11:46,733 --> 00:11:50,700
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

256
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:54,700
<i> Brother, is that blood?</i>

257
00:11:55,667 --> 00:11:57,100
<i> There was a...</i>

258
00:11:57,233 --> 00:11:59,800
<i> a branch on the driveway.</i>

259
00:12:00,233 --> 00:12:02,233
<i> I wasn't looking.</i>

260
00:12:02,367 --> 00:12:06,500
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

261
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:24,033
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

262
00:12:36,100 --> 00:12:38,233
I want you to keep
an eye on Delgado.

263
00:12:39,100 --> 00:12:41,967
All the movements of him
and his men.

264
00:12:42,100 --> 00:12:43,400
<i> Copy, Berdugo.</i>

265
00:12:43,633 --> 00:12:45,167
I'll watch them.

266
00:12:45,300 --> 00:12:48,267
What if I just have
that Korean obliterated?

267
00:12:48,433 --> 00:12:50,500
He's the only thorn
in my throat,

268
00:12:51,033 --> 00:12:52,800
but he's heavily guarded now.

269
00:12:53,033 --> 00:12:53,800
Too risky.

270
00:12:53,933 --> 00:12:55,500
We'll wait for the right timing.

271
00:12:55,633 --> 00:12:57,267
<i> It's your call, Berdugo.</i>

272
00:12:57,400 --> 00:13:00,300
I'm ready anytime.

273
00:13:00,433 --> 00:13:04,433
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

274
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:20,833
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

275
00:13:33,867 --> 00:13:35,300
[CLICKS]

276
00:13:35,700 --> 00:13:39,867
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

277
00:13:48,900 --> 00:13:51,367
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

278
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:54,100
[KEYS CLICKING]

279
00:14:08,767 --> 00:14:11,033
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

280
00:14:31,933 --> 00:14:37,300
[CLICKING]

281
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:49,367
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

282
00:14:59,767 --> 00:15:09,433
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

283
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:15,933
[PHONE BUZZING]

284
00:15:17,967 --> 00:15:27,933
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

285
00:15:31,067 --> 00:15:33,200
<i>There's a group moving towards
the parking area.</i>

286
00:15:33,333 --> 00:15:34,133
<i> It could be Berdugo.</i>

287
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:35,300
<i> Intercept!</i>

288
00:15:35,433 --> 00:15:37,300
- [GUN FIRING]
- [TOMAS GROANS]

289
00:15:39,167 --> 00:15:43,300
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

290
00:15:57,567 --> 00:16:02,067
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

291
00:16:20,067 --> 00:16:24,100
[CURIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

292
00:16:36,267 --> 00:16:40,367
[♪STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING♪]

293
00:16:55,567 --> 00:16:57,200
What are you saying?

294
00:16:57,833 --> 00:17:00,533
Matias, he's not Berdugo?

295
00:17:01,567 --> 00:17:03,100
Yes.

296
00:17:03,533 --> 00:17:05,267
You have the wrong person.

297
00:17:05,867 --> 00:17:07,767
If he's not Berdugo,

298
00:17:08,533 --> 00:17:10,500
then who is?

299
00:17:12,033 --> 00:17:14,500
I'm not joking with you.

300
00:17:14,633 --> 00:17:18,867
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

301
00:17:21,933 --> 00:17:23,467
Oh, Andrew...

302
00:17:23,600 --> 00:17:24,933
I was trying to call you.

303
00:17:25,067 --> 00:17:27,567
Ah, I didn't know
that you were coming.

304
00:17:30,433 --> 00:17:32,333
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

305
00:17:32,467 --> 00:17:34,100
Yvette, have you noticed
anything unusual

306
00:17:34,233 --> 00:17:36,367
about Tomas lately?

307
00:17:37,733 --> 00:17:39,267
What do you mean?

308
00:17:39,800 --> 00:17:42,100
Something unusual,
something off?

309
00:17:43,967 --> 00:17:46,533
Well...

310
00:17:46,667 --> 00:17:49,867
earlier, at the precinct
and lately, he's been tense.

311
00:17:50,667 --> 00:17:51,600
Ah...

312
00:17:51,733 --> 00:17:53,733
and the other day,
he raised his voice at me.

313
00:17:53,867 --> 00:17:55,333
That's not like him.

314
00:17:56,067 --> 00:17:59,267
And then he's very impatient
and distracted.

315
00:17:59,400 --> 00:18:01,233
Turns out he's stressed

316
00:18:01,367 --> 00:18:04,833
because of this whole Matias
situation and the business.

317
00:18:05,333 --> 00:18:06,500
But you know, I mean...

318
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:09,933
He's been dragged
into something illegal.

319
00:18:10,067 --> 00:18:12,900
I mean, you know,
anyone would be shaken.

320
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:16,333
Why are you asking?

321
00:18:16,467 --> 00:18:17,967
Andrew?

322
00:18:19,533 --> 00:18:23,400
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

323
00:18:23,567 --> 00:18:25,267
I didn't expect to see you here.

324
00:18:26,100 --> 00:18:29,800
I came here to check on you,
Tomas.

325
00:18:30,833 --> 00:18:34,467
Of course,
after what happened...

326
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:36,700
after Berdugo was caught, right?

327
00:18:37,233 --> 00:18:39,067
That's very thoughtful of you,
brother-in-law,

328
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:40,467
but I'm fine.

329
00:18:41,800 --> 00:18:44,900
In fact, it's you
I want to check on.

330
00:18:45,733 --> 00:18:47,767
You and your friends,

331
00:18:47,900 --> 00:18:50,067
you must all feel
very relieved...

332
00:18:50,667 --> 00:18:53,333
Now that Berdugo
has been caught, right?

333
00:18:53,467 --> 00:18:56,333
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

334
00:18:59,433 --> 00:19:01,067
Well, I haven't seen them yet.

335
00:19:02,033 --> 00:19:04,133
Since Matias was caught,

336
00:19:06,433 --> 00:19:09,267
there hasn't been any reason
for me to meet them, Tomas.

337
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:11,733
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

338
00:19:11,967 --> 00:19:14,167
I'm focused on work, on...

339
00:19:14,733 --> 00:19:16,167
Tirada,

340
00:19:16,900 --> 00:19:17,967
family.

341
00:19:18,533 --> 00:19:19,400
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

342
00:19:19,533 --> 00:19:20,933
Like now, I will...

343
00:19:21,467 --> 00:19:23,600
just say good night to my nieces
and nephews.

344
00:19:26,800 --> 00:19:28,800
- Yvette.
- Okay.

345
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:33,833
Hon, I'll just have them
prepare dinner, okay?

346
00:19:33,967 --> 00:19:35,333
Okay.

347
00:19:35,467 --> 00:19:39,767
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

348
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:43,633
Is there something
you're not telling me?

349
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:46,400
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

350
00:19:46,533 --> 00:19:49,033
Dad, let's just wait for Andrew.

351
00:19:49,333 --> 00:19:51,367
What does Andrew have
to do with this?

352
00:19:52,233 --> 00:19:54,300
He's just looking for something,
Uncle.

353
00:19:55,233 --> 00:19:58,033
He's getting evidence.

354
00:19:58,167 --> 00:19:59,700
What evidence?

355
00:20:01,300 --> 00:20:03,367
You know we are just wasting
time here!

356
00:20:04,233 --> 00:20:06,133
Yes, that is what I am saying.

357
00:20:08,133 --> 00:20:09,633
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

358
00:20:09,767 --> 00:20:11,800
Dad, let's trust Andrew.

359
00:20:12,833 --> 00:20:15,767
He's already done a lot for us.

360
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:19,100
This is the only thing he's
asking for, just a little time.

361
00:20:19,967 --> 00:20:22,300
And he's on his way.

362
00:20:23,833 --> 00:20:25,567
[CLOCK TICKING]

363
00:20:25,700 --> 00:20:27,500
I don't understand you...

364
00:20:29,667 --> 00:20:31,367
but I will do as you ask.

365
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:35,467
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

366
00:20:41,433 --> 00:20:43,167
Oh, Uncle Andrew.

367
00:20:43,300 --> 00:20:45,033
Ah, Harris.

368
00:20:45,333 --> 00:20:47,567
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

369
00:20:47,700 --> 00:20:49,133
Are you still doing your
homework?

370
00:20:49,267 --> 00:20:50,800
Ah, I'm almost done, Uncle.

371
00:20:50,933 --> 00:20:52,867
So I can play the new video game

372
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:54,167
I want to play.

373
00:20:54,300 --> 00:20:56,033
Do you want to join?

374
00:20:56,600 --> 00:20:57,467
Next time.

375
00:20:58,967 --> 00:21:00,233
Oh, by the way,

376
00:21:00,367 --> 00:21:03,267
the reason I came here is
because I have a question.

377
00:21:04,100 --> 00:21:05,300
Do you still remember
the teddy bear

378
00:21:05,433 --> 00:21:07,300
you would always show me?

379
00:21:08,133 --> 00:21:09,800
Is it still here?

380
00:21:09,967 --> 00:21:14,400
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

381
00:21:17,433 --> 00:21:21,633
["NEVER SAY DIE" INSTRUMENTAL
PLAYING]

382
00:21:24,267 --> 00:21:25,600
We're going to the rest house

383
00:21:25,733 --> 00:21:26,867
to visit Mommy.

384
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:27,567
I'll go with you guys.

385
00:21:27,700 --> 00:21:29,533
Major, this is Andrew.

386
00:21:30,600 --> 00:21:32,367
Brother Tomas went with them.

387
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:33,933
Andrew, you go in first.

388
00:21:34,067 --> 00:21:34,967
Bring your car.

389
00:21:35,100 --> 00:21:36,867
Secure your family.

390
00:21:40,567 --> 00:21:43,733
[GUN FIRING]

391
00:21:43,900 --> 00:21:45,300
Dad...
